        "description": {
            "value": "<p>You send a brutal signal interruption straight into the central processor of a technological being. This signal wreaks havoc on the system and leaves behind lasting corruption. The target takes 15d8 mental damage, or electricity damage, if the target is immune to mental damage. Beings that are biomechanical (such as androids) or only partially mechanical (such as cyborgs) uses the outcome for one degree of success better than the result of their saving throw.</p><hr /><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature is unaffected.</p>\n<p><strong>Success</strong> The creature takes half damage and becomes @UUID[Compendium.sf2e.conditions.Item.Glitching]{Glitching 1}.</p>\n<p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature takes full damage and becomes @UUID[Compendium.sf2e.conditions.Item.Glitching]{Glitching 2} and @UUID[Compendium.sf2e.conditions.Item.Stunned]{Stunned 1}.</p>\n<p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The creature takes double damage, becomes @UUID[Compendium.sf2e.conditions.Item.Glitching]{Glitching 3} and @UUID[Compendium.sf2e.conditions.Item.Stunned]{Stunned 2}, and must succeed at a Fortitude save or suffer catastrophic systems failure. This kills any creature reliant on technology to live. This Fortitude save has the death and incapacitation traits.</p>"
        },
